* Sat Oct 17 2026 Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com> - 1.0.1-1
- The feature file was not well-formed XML: its comment contained "--",
  which XML forbids inside a comment. Android 13's parser tolerated it, so
  nothing changed on bigtab01, but a strict parser would reject the file and
  the feature would be silently absent. Found by tests/policy.py's new xml
  check. The declaration itself is unchanged.

* Thu Sep 24 2026 Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com> - 1.0.0-1
- First package. One file, and the one that makes the other three Wi-Fi
  packages mean anything.
- Recommends rather than Requires waydroid-ext-wifid, so that the Stage 0
  configuration -- feature declared, nothing behind it -- stays installable.
  That is how the no-vendor-HAL question was answered.
